      "item_body": "<p>[K/U] Each graph is the graph of the derivative f'(x) of a function f(x). For each graph, determine i. the interval(s) on which f is increasing; ii. the interval(s) on which f is decreasing; iii. the x-coordinate(s) of any local extrema of f. Then, assuming f(0) = 2, make a rough sketch of f.</p>\n<p><img id=\"55741\" src=\"https://inst-fs-iad-prod.inscloudgate.net/files/7839b232-12b8-4ff0-b2e7-ceb57936f38c/ex41_q9.png?token=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiIsImtpZCI6Im5ldy1xdWl6emVzL21haW4ifQ..SQEtDIH82pe5LyqOMA8Rsiiejbic0_70loY--wFapm6icoea4ylay4gFEjOR2p5onHxoMEW1IA4XWOPUDBkchw\" alt=\"ex41_q9.png\" data-old-link=\"/courses/905/files/55741/preview\"></p>\n<p>a. graph a: f is increasing on <span id=\"blank_3818dbf0-cb2e-46e5-84dc-bb52ca611cf3\"></span>; f is decreasing on <span id=\"blank_8960b56a-6054-4567-b878-34d5283115b1\"></span>; local extremum at x = <span id=\"blank_7663d34c-879d-42fa-befb-b4e256b4fbb5\"></span></p>\n<p>b. graph b: f is increasing on <span id=\"blank_a8babafc-c0ff-41ed-9349-b252ba4d9ee5\"></span>; f is decreasing on <span id=\"blank_5e5ad41c-f9c2-4431-80d6-1550af62e160\"></span>; local extrema at x = <span id=\"blank_267195f5-8a7e-4037-934c-c9dc2b59ff31\"></span> and <span id=\"blank_1e6de521-5b35-4291-a862-9516b125180a\"></span></p>\n<p>c. graph c: f is increasing on <span id=\"blank_6531e858-4c3d-4692-b501-cc5957f46a18\"></span>; f is decreasing on <span id=\"blank_2c142aa6-d685-4f72-87d8-af3edeee304a\"></span>; local extrema at x = <span id=\"blank_5f9bd3b8-597f-42fb-8bf8-43c1ee222bac\"></span> and <span id=\"blank_1a0dd179-c861-4f6b-ad84-0f19d128eab2\"></span></p>\n<p>d. graph d: f is increasing on <span id=\"blank_fd1c2441-75b0-4b91-af34-74ecae24122b\"></span>; f is decreasing on <span id=\"blank_4e61a3a7-b263-4c89-be16-69a26cf83f05\"></span>; local extremum at x = <span id=\"blank_bd104121-3813-49c1-bf60-25531b84ef72\"></span></p>",
